      "notes": "### 5D Sensory Pentagon [2, 2, 2]\n- **1. Behavior (Rigid Shift-Work):** Monotonous bells, repetitive marching cadence — *Rule:* Stepping out of foot traffic causes civic bottleneck.\n- **2. Relationship (Tiered Bureaucracy):** Triplicate requisition vouchers, stamped badges — *Rule:* Forged seals or stolen passes are 100% effective.\n- **3. Attitude (Suspicious Scapegoating):** Outsiders undergo strip searches and quarantine tolls — *Rule:* Minor infractions prompt heavy extortion fines.\n- **4. Values (The Law's Letter):** *Sacred:* The statute book and protocol manual | *Expendable:* Human comfort and individual innocence\n- **5. Environment (Fortified Panopticon):** Cold dressed granite, searchlights, smelling of lye and bleach — *Rule:* Stealth checks suffer disadvantage due to open sightlines.\n\n### 5D Sensory Pentagon [2, 2, 2]\n- **1. Behavior (Pragmatic Routine):** Low murmur of trade, sizzling food stalls — *Rule:* Standard stealth and rumor-gathering work normally.\n- **2. Relationship (Mercenary Contract):** Itemized invoices, debt tallies on noticeboards — *Rule:* Gold or valuable salvage buys access to highest council.\n- **3. Attitude (Lethal Paranoia):** Outsiders assumed to be foreign saboteurs — *Rule:* Failed social check results in immediate arrest.\n- **4. Values (The Law's Letter):** *Sacred:* The statute book and protocol manual | *Expendable:* Human comfort and individual innocence\n- **5. Environment (Fortified Panopticon):** Cold dressed granite, searchlights, smelling of lye and bleach — *Rule:* Stealth checks suffer disadvantage due to open sightlines."
